  "reason": "The records supply several important ingredients but not their decisive connection. R1, R8, and R13 establish the relevance of FCC/B2 lamellar eutectic structures in closely related Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni alloys; R2, R4, and R18 show that combined pressure and temperature can alter phase stability in an HEA; and R7 shows substantial processing-induced phase and microstructural evolution in AlCoCrFeNi. Most importantly, R3 and R12 describe coherent interfaces or coherent lamellae transmitting dislocations, relieving stress concentrations, and suppressing cracking, while R5, R10, R14, and R16 support the contribution of faults, twins, and transformations to plasticity. However, none shows HPHT converting the target FCC/B2 lamellae into a hierarchical coherent-interface architecture, and R3 even limits its comparison with brittle B2-containing systems. Thus the literature points toward pressure/temperature microstructure engineering and the desired coherent-interface mechanism, but choosing HPHT for this eutectic alloy and predicting the specific hierarchical transformation would still require a substantial new idea."
